gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;a03210d5dcca87b0eab1396bd60751d0cd577941;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;549;0;0;    if (pmeActive && pmeRunMode != PmeRunMode::GPU && (isDomainDecomposition || havePmeOnlyRank));I think the main issue here is that pmeRunMode is not correct. I have a small WIP change just uploaded to fix that. _  _ If we have that fixed, than I think what this condition can include a check for _ (pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::None) instead of passing a new boolean.
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;a03210d5dcca87b0eab1396bd60751d0cd577941;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;549;0;0;    if (pmeActive && pmeRunMode != PmeRunMode::GPU && (isDomainDecomposition || havePmeOnlyRank));Thanks Alan. I have uploaded patch set 2.
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;a03210d5dcca87b0eab1396bd60751d0cd577941;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;549;0;0;    if (pmeActive && pmeRunMode != PmeRunMode::GPU && (isDomainDecomposition || havePmeOnlyRank));I suggest you rebase this change onto https://gerrit.gromacs.org/c/gromacs/+/15285. To do this (at least one way), checkout 15285 and then cherry-pick this change onto it (where the commands to check-out and cherry-pick can be pasted from the respective gerrit "Download Patch" menu). Then make and locally commit any further edits and squash this further commit into the cherry-pick commit before pushing to gerrit in the ame way as before. Since the Change-ID in the commit message will then be the same as previously, gerrit will recognise this as being a new patch-set to the same change. Let me know if you need any help.
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;a03210d5dcca87b0eab1396bd60751d0cd577941;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;549;0;0;    if (pmeActive && pmeRunMode != PmeRunMode::GPU && (isDomainDecomposition || havePmeOnlyRank));I agree. Setting pmeRunMode will be a better fix. So, should I wait for your fix to be available in release branch before I make this change?
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);While this does give the desired behavior, I find it really hard to parse, I guess mostly because there are implicit assumptions here (e.g. how does the havePmeOnlyRank relate to GPU update). _  _ @Artem: Couldn't we simply check that if either of the GPU comm dev flags is set, PME should be offloaded for update to be offloadable.
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);> In any case, very few will ever see these messages, so no point in tinkering a lot with these. _  _ My concern here is that if a user ever did get one of these messages, it would be very unclear what they need to do in order to resolve the problem. We should at least say something about whether/which mdp or command line options the user might tinker with to resolve the error state.
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);> Also, I think you are missing isDomainDecomposition flag. But this is another question: what should we do if one sets GPU halo exchange or GPU PP comms envvars when there is no DD? _  _ OK, in that case ideally checks like (devFlags.enableGpuHaloExchange && isDomainDecomposition) would be far better for clarity. I don't like that limitations of the GPU direct communication are implicitly encoded in the checks and error messages which end up confusing (i.e. it is not that "With domain decomposition, PME must run fully on the GPU." but that "With domain decomposition, as only direct comm is supported together with GPU update, PME must be run on the GPU"). _  _ In any case, very few will ever see these messages, so no point in tinkering a lot with these. _  _ More importantly, control variables like devFlags.enableGpuHaloExchange should preferably have values consistent with the rest of the run setup (i.e. checks manageDevelopmentFeatures() whether the run actually has DD or separate PME), but if we want to allow inconsistent env vars to be passed and then overridden (e.g. GMX_GPU_DD_COMMS to a single-rank run) than at least when setting up SimulationWorkload we should do correct overrides and not end up with inconsistent workload flags (which afaict we now do).
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);Done
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);By looking to this with fresh eyes I would agree: It is hard to parse. I think the reason is that there are two completely different conditions combined in one here. One checks if PME is offloaded and the second checks if there is actually PME. You are forgetting non-PME case in your assumption (that is exactly what I did and why this change is here now).
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);I think this is way better! Thanks, Mark.
gromacs~release-2020~Ic49f99b2e2afddabd7e2c8e68ab3d6d9325dc07a;0fdb424aa2751ff490b23f5b9cf4ae5976244fe5;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;580;579;580;    if ((pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed);How about _  _  /* If PME is active (ie not PmeRunMode::None), then GPU update requires _   * either a single-rank run, or that PME runs fully on the GPU. */ _  const bool pmeRunningOnCpu = (pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::CPU || pmeRunMode == PmeRunMode::Mixed)_ _  if (pmeRunningOnCpu && isDomainDecomposition) _  { _    errorMessage += "With domain decomposition, PME must run fully on the GPU.\n"_ _  } _  if (pmeRunningOnCpu && havePmeOnlyRank) _  { _    errorMessage += "With separate PME rank(s), PME must run fully on the GPU.\n"_ _  }
