gromacs~release-2020~Ie6b076c4309c7695ab9b46037ced92e95dea1558;20e1789d5e92b2fa093c510af95fa9af1f110fa7;src/gromacs/taskassignment/reportgpuusage.cpp;150;0;0;                                    useGpuForUpdate ? "GPU" : "CPU")_;We need to better consider how do we communicate task assignment to users. We extended the scope of "PP task" to include bondeds with the reasoning that PP ranks have bondeds too. With the same reasoning (i.e. update is part of the "PP task"), this too should be listed on the message constructed on lines 139-140.
gromacs~release-2020~Ie6b076c4309c7695ab9b46037ced92e95dea1558;20e1789d5e92b2fa093c510af95fa9af1f110fa7;src/gromacs/taskassignment/reportgpuusage.cpp;150;0;0;                                    useGpuForUpdate ? "GPU" : "CPU")_;By the message doe not say anything about the tasks. Should we instead consider updating documentation?
gromacs~release-2020~Ie6b076c4309c7695ab9b46037ced92e95dea1558;20e1789d5e92b2fa093c510af95fa9af1f110fa7;src/gromacs/taskassignment/reportgpuusage.cpp;150;0;0;                                    useGpuForUpdate ? "GPU" : "CPU")_;> Did not get this. Why update is a part of PP task? Because it is in (PME-)PP rank (not in PME-only rank)? _  _ Our documentation only refers to "PP task" and "PME task" so it is now inconsistent in that it neither tells the user that there is a new "GPU task" that has to be mapped with the "-gputask" option nor does it document that this new task is part of the PP task and it is mapped with the respective identifier in the "-gputasks" specifier.  _  _ Historiically, PP and PME are the two offload "task" entities that can have GPUs assigned to_ when bondeds were added, as the PP/PME rank split aligns well with the offload task to GPU mapping, we maintained that wording. Hence, we print the deviceId to "task" mapping as, e.g. "PP:0" or "PP:0,PME:0" (see the "-gputasks" entry under http://manual.gromacs.org/documentation/current/user-guide/mdrun-performance.html#running-mdrun-within-a-single-node) and the text below this mapping hints which tasks are offloaded. _  _ As we have not added a separate designator for the "update-constraints" tasks, we either need to add one (i.e. something like "PP:0,PME:0,UPDATE:0") or document that this is part of the PP task and print it consistently.
