gromacs~master~Ia1f709a90472a95ad76af92c41df570ba7c28255;ea72913378b7c41fbf45e37e98c7925082b2ac7b;src/gromacs/pbcutil/pbc.h;56;53;56;#    undef None;Does anyone have a better idea on how to solve the X11 issue?  _ Other solutions i came up with: _ - Include the pbc.h in several files (3-4 files) of programs/view so that this file will be parsed before the X11/x.h _ - Rename None into something else.
gromacs~master~Ia1f709a90472a95ad76af92c41df570ba7c28255;ea72913378b7c41fbf45e37e98c7925082b2ac7b;src/gromacs/pbcutil/pbc.h;56;53;56;#ifdef None;It's a composite problem - view has types and functions that need both X11 types like Window and the gmx PbcType, and functions that use macros declared in pbc.h (which has too many different kinds of things declared in it), and view makes too much use of headers including other headers rather than using forward declarations (which is why people get code review comments from me to avoid doing that). Removing the compact unit cell stuff from pbc.h helps a little, as would working out how to separate the X11 calls from the higher level code in view so that a gmx type that contains Window can be insulated from the other code. _  _ But for now, Magnus suggestion makes sense.
