gromacs~release-2020~I7317d83271158c9973f4c102d8ca830b437626b5;772ab572cec456710730ecde571d11149a31d51e;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;630;0;0;                    "by the GMX_FORCE_UPDATE_DEFAULT_GPU environment variable,\n";Actually this is inconsistent. If the env var forces GPU update, then we should give an error because we can't do what was required. if the env var changes the implementation of auto, then we should be consistent with all the other times we decide to run on the CPU, and not issue a warning. The user had the option of using both the env var and the -update flag, and didn't force things on the GPU, so they're ok with gmx choosing not to run the update on the GPU. _  _ that the env var has no docs in the user guide section is another problem here
