gromacs~release-2020~Ie7f03f5beea2d78411c7a0cdfa85f71deeb622fa;050b1367dd72a493a893cc7ffb174026e817a62e;src/gromacs/modularsimulator/statepropagatordata.h;295;292;295;    //! Count of input file options (used for final output only).;This is implementing mdrun -c, which only works at the last step. It's co-located with the trajectory and checkpoint output in do_md_trajectory_writing() because they all need to gather the global state. We need to be efficient about that during the simulation, but for mdrun -c it is not important to be efficient while doing final-step I/O. _  _ It would be much better to pass the result of ftp2fn(efSTO, nfile_, fnm_) into the constructor and store std::string finalConfigurationFilename_, rather than keep handles to t_filenm. Or better, opt2fn("-c", nfile, fnm). That limits the dependencies we need to add to implement this class.
