gromacs~release-2020~Iceb9aac395335c062109d552d3f0289688a9c75f;40cd86c216b1876e72f5799b552f2600603a6b24;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;1701;0;0;                // Note: AtomLocality::All is used for the non-DD case because, as in this;I don't understand at all. I suggest more like: _  _ With DD, the CPU force H2D transfer has to run in the local stream so that it does not affect force halo exchange operations(?). However, without DD this problem does not arise, so we can overlap the CPU force H2D transfer with the GPU force work in the local stream (and any others?) better if we use the stream for AtomLocality::All (ie the update stream). _  _ but perhaps I haven't understood everything correctly.
