gromacs~master~Ib4b7f5f0e57b82c939f53e9805dc16e9d76db22b;6036fc5d59c3f3519af3ae23f51cadc40ad587f0;src/gromacs/utility/listoflists.h;54;0;0;/*! \brief A list of lists, optimized for performance;imo what we want is something with the interface of a ragged 2D vector (so the class interface has things like you'd see on std::vector<std::vector<int>>, including operator[], begin(), end(), and size(), that return things like or related to ArrayRef<int>). We implement that like nice (called a flattened, or Iliffe array - see Wikipedia) and also exposing new methods that return views of the flattened array for the times that we consume it like that. There is a risk that listOfLists[ai] is ambiguous to humans (is it an integer from the flattened array, or a view from the 2D ragged one?) but not to compilers. So that might motivate an interface like Berk proposes. But I see that idea has changed.
