gromacs~release-2019~Ic697f596285acdb5c7728b7ebc995ea44c82f3ac;325dc2b72d9bbe2ca8cd49b43489b95af9f5b589;src/api/cpp/CMakeLists.txt;96;0;0;;The defaults seem to be okay for the current configuration of the top-level CMakeLists.txt and tests.
gromacs~release-2019~Ic697f596285acdb5c7728b7ebc995ea44c82f3ac;325dc2b72d9bbe2ca8cd49b43489b95af9f5b589;src/api/cpp/CMakeLists.txt;99;0;0;# Install and export gmxapi and Gromacs::gmxapi.;We should check that this does something sensible on a mac. Eric is working on a package of stuff we could have in Jenkins, but for now we need a human to do a manual test.
gromacs~release-2019~Ic697f596285acdb5c7728b7ebc995ea44c82f3ac;325dc2b72d9bbe2ca8cd49b43489b95af9f5b589;src/api/cpp/CMakeLists.txt;99;0;0;# Install and export gmxapi and Gromacs::gmxapi.;Yes, with CMake 3.9 and policy CMP0068 active, `set_target_properties(gmxapi PROPERTIES INSTALL_NAME_DIR "\@rpath")` became the correct way to set the install name to `@rpath/libgmxapi.0.dylib` whereas previously it could happen as a side effect of RPATH settings, which is inappropriate. So this property setting should remain, but the other non-default settings you remove in this patch are fine as a result of that previous change you reference, along with the followup change I submitted a while back to change @executable_path to @loader_path. _  _ Tested with CMake 3.10 for CMP0068 on and off, which should cover the pre-3.9 CMake use case as well. _  _ For additional annotation, how about: _ "Explicitly specify library install name so that the correct loading instruction is produced in client code. Client code should be able to find the library relative to the client code RPATH. Without explicitly specifying, INSTALL_NAME_DIR is inherited from the global CMAKE_INSTALL_NAME_DIR, which is not appropriate for libgmxapi if it uses an install name relative to the executable_path or loader_path."
gromacs~release-2019~Ic697f596285acdb5c7728b7ebc995ea44c82f3ac;325dc2b72d9bbe2ca8cd49b43489b95af9f5b589;src/api/cpp/CMakeLists.txt;99;0;0;# Install and export gmxapi and Gromacs::gmxapi.;This is necessary so that libgmxapi.dylib identifies itself as @rpath/libgmxapi.0.dylib instead of  @loader_path/../lib/libgmxapi.0.dylib
gromacs~release-2019~Ic697f596285acdb5c7728b7ebc995ea44c82f3ac;325dc2b72d9bbe2ca8cd49b43489b95af9f5b589;src/api/cpp/CMakeLists.txt;99;0;0;# Install and export gmxapi and Gromacs::gmxapi.;OK. With which version of cmake? Per https://cmake.org/cmake/help/v3.9/policy/CMP0068.html, once we have cmake 3.9 (which is already proposed as the minimum for the 2020 series) then perhaps we need nothing at all. If so, I suggest we retain this, and leave a comment that we can remove it when we require cmake >= 3.9. _  _ See also https://redmine.gromacs.org/projects/gromacs/repository/revisions/a726027aa49762378558291c1d88ebf2fb611200/diff/CMakeLists.txt in case that enlightens
gromacs~release-2019~Ic697f596285acdb5c7728b7ebc995ea44c82f3ac;325dc2b72d9bbe2ca8cd49b43489b95af9f5b589;src/api/cpp/CMakeLists.txt;103;0;0;# add to their include path to be able to `#include "gmxapi/some_header.h"`;This does not appear to be necessary in the current environment.
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;f8a8252cd2a4b7760167cbbce3dc3474ae1534e1;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;1055;0;0;            !thisRankHasDuty(cr, DUTY_PME) && !simulationWork.useGpuPmePpCommunication_;duty has an incomplete implementation dating from ages ago. All ranks have pme duty by default, regardless of coulombtype(!), and that only changes if a pme rank is used. So rf simulations have all ranks with pme duty, from that default. So the answer to Artem's first question is that this bool is false.
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;This unneeded check is still here.
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;I already explained why it's needed
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;But the check is even incorrect, as it doesn't check for F_CONSTRNC.
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;I don't care about efficiency here. I would like to code to be intelligible.
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;But then I prefer it the other way around. _ hasAnyConstraints should only check interaction count. _ The shake check can then do hasAnyConstraints && (gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0)
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;OK that way is a bit more efficient
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;it is used on 524 and allow not to call gmx_mtop_interaction_count(...) on 513. Although i did not see much point in it apart of making these checks more self-explanatory
gromacs~release-2020~I57e3ad3b8a571ec244989e888afd5cfcbaf9b75e;2466c4074fd7fc94cd14d2f08db17909b5858462;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;511;0;0;    const bool hasConstrainedBonds = gmx_mtop_ftype_count(mtop, F_CONSTR) > 0_;Not sure which version is better. I think we should go with readability in this part of the code.
