gromacs~release-2020~I1a2052968c8d8dd8020744bf15f974bc0d92a6ef;5dcd71e0100439fc33cb3a7bb427525b85860638;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;579;578;579;    //       when update auto chooses GPU in some cases. Currently exceeding the restriction;t_inputrec contains no information about constraints. _ A small routine is needed to compute the number of coupled constraints. Ideally it should use the same code that use now used for CUDA LINCS to compute this count and generate the fatal error.
gromacs~release-2020~I1a2052968c8d8dd8020744bf15f974bc0d92a6ef;5dcd71e0100439fc33cb3a7bb427525b85860638;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;579;578;579;    //       when update auto chooses GPU in some cases. Currently exceeding the restriction;Not per se (IIRC settle, shake and lincs are all supported). There should be something about whether update groups are supported with the user's input, when it's a DD run, because all-bonds constraints uses iterative LINCS which would generally not be performant with a GPU. In principle, all-bonds can work with a single PP rank, but I don't know if we implemented/tested that.
gromacs~release-2020~I1a2052968c8d8dd8020744bf15f974bc0d92a6ef;5dcd71e0100439fc33cb3a7bb427525b85860638;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidegpuusage.cpp;579;578;579;    //       when update auto chooses GPU in some cases. Currently exceeding the restriction;The CUDA LINCS code supports coupled constraints up to the block size, which is currently 256. So H-bond only constraints will always work and systems with all-bonds constrained will work with molecules up to 257 atoms. _ As the message says, we need a check for the coupled constraint count if we want to enable auto to choose GPU update.
