gromacs~release-2020~Ib41e012b9f56591c80046b44891dd77af5a2f938;d359c2f6979c9c64033c5d154b88d769ddbe5b15;src/gromacs/taskassignment/taskassignment.cpp;357;0;0;        gmx_fatal(FARGS,;Under all other conditions one rank will exit before both barriers and no rank will get through the last barrier.
gromacs~release-2020~Ib41e012b9f56591c80046b44891dd77af5a2f938;d359c2f6979c9c64033c5d154b88d769ddbe5b15;src/gromacs/taskassignment/taskassignment.cpp;357;0;0;        gmx_fatal(FARGS,;I was not suggesting to change the order, but to have an additional simulationBarrier() call before the multisim one. Then no PP rank can get through the barrier when a PP rank issues a fatal warning. That is the goal, right?
gromacs~release-2020~Ib41e012b9f56591c80046b44891dd77af5a2f938;d359c2f6979c9c64033c5d154b88d769ddbe5b15;src/gromacs/taskassignment/taskassignment.cpp;357;0;0;        gmx_fatal(FARGS,;So final question: Do we want to catch those cases in a barrier? _ Putting a simulationBarrier(cr) before the multiSimBarrier would catch all cases except for non-PP ranks failing.
