gromacs~release-2020~Ib41e012b9f56591c80046b44891dd77af5a2f938;d359c2f6979c9c64033c5d154b88d769ddbe5b15;src/gromacs/taskassignment/taskassignment.cpp;357;0;0;        gmx_fatal(FARGS,;The barriers work for the reason commented on line 348. (Jenkins had lots of false negatives because gmxtest.pl couldn't find the text in mdrun.out that it needs in order to decide how to try alternatives, because some other rank got to exit() before stderr got written/flushed. Delaying the exit() is the necessary thing.) _  _ Changing the order of 353 and 354 doesn't affect whether any rank did anything on line 337. Barriers impede progress, they don't ensure exceptions have been expressed to the user.
gromacs~release-2020~Ib41e012b9f56591c80046b44891dd77af5a2f938;d359c2f6979c9c64033c5d154b88d769ddbe5b15;src/gromacs/taskassignment/taskassignment.cpp;357;0;0;        gmx_fatal(FARGS,;No rank can get through the existing barrier. The goal is to let a node-master rank that has an exception issue its error message and then exit before any other rank reaches any exit that might pre-empt the message. Any kind of global barrier does that. _  _ Further, note that PP vs PME rank doesn't matter here, all ranks are running this code.
