gromacs~release-2020~I768898839e5c6a653894d5eb80354f0e423e06ed;84a2acb289bd728bdd3433f9df58d21eb1dc0106;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;1598;0;0;                gpuHaloExchange->communicateHaloForces(haveCpuLocalForces)_;This is a pre-existing issue relating to how we construct the list of dependencies, so should not be addressed in this change. _  _ In the long term, it would be simpler to add the synchronizer to the list at this point, rather than have to copy the logic leading to line 1592 in order to correctly depend on the synchronizer only when needed. I don't have a clear sense of whether that's best to do by constructing gpuHaloExchange with the handle to the list to append to, or passing that handle here, or returning a handle to the synchronizer to add to the list. All of them remove the code smell that is the getter for the thing to add to the list. If I had to guess now, i'd pass that handle here, so that the possible dependency is clear at this level.
gromacs~release-2020~I768898839e5c6a653894d5eb80354f0e423e06ed;84a2acb289bd728bdd3433f9df58d21eb1dc0106;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;1598;0;0;                gpuHaloExchange->communicateHaloForces(haveCpuLocalForces)_;I agree, the conditional should not be repeated below. We decided to make dependency handlingclear in the schedule (rather than passing pointers to synchronizes to a constructor), especially for reductions. If we figure out a better way (with code) to avoid using a stale / out-of-date synchronizer object (which is unfortunately too easy with CUDA), we could go back to constructing gpuHaloExchange and other objects with synchronizers.
gromacs~release-2020~I768898839e5c6a653894d5eb80354f0e423e06ed;84a2acb289bd728bdd3433f9df58d21eb1dc0106;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;1701;0;0;        gmx::FixedCapacityVector<GpuEventSynchronizer*, 3> dependencyList_;If someone agrees with my point above, then perhaps a TODO above this would make sense to suggest e.g. creating a gpuForceDependencyList high up, and passing that to the functions that call the things that create the synchronizers, rather than asking the things for their synchronizers and needing to do so only when valid. See https://martinfowler.com/bliki/TellDontAsk.html
