gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;6;0;0;AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: false;You refer to this problem: https://llvm.org/bugs/show_bug.cgi?id=27353 ? If we want to use clang-format before this is fixed and want align we could use left align instead.
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;6;0;0;AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: false;I take back my suggestion of Left. If one declares multiple pointers on one line, than it switches back to Right even if it set to Left which makes it inconsistent. I'm also not a big fan of Right with alignment after the pointer. But I think it's the best option because it preserves alignment and is consistent.
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;6;0;0;AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: false;I don't care what value we put there. I changed this to true. With some other changes in patch set 2, the difference between uncrustify and clang-format is "only" ~50k lines. I left PointerAlignment=Right to make comparison easier, but there probably is an option in uncrustify to get also the other option.
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;20;0;0;BinPackArguments: true;This and below would probably be better as false.
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;20;0;0;BinPackArguments: true;I take that back, I read the documentation incorrectly.
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;34;0;0;BreakBeforeBinaryOperators: All;This behaves somewhat annoyingly in that if the code does not follow the setting set here, it joins the lines (or does something else that is quite unpredictable).
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;ca5a5c82247a5754a1eebb25a0b842a3432cef2e;.clang-format;34;0;0;BreakBeforeBinaryOperators: All;If we want to go with clang-format, we should pick one value for this, and then use uncrustify to move all the operators to follow the chosen convention before applying clang-format. That probably has least impact to the existing line breaks. This applies to all kinds of binary operators, probably including all of assignment, logical, and arithmetic. It may also include = 0 in pure virtual method definitions...
