gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;e0732ba1b116a0929696e6523168900b491c0b3c;.clang-format;3;0;0;AccessModifierOffset: -4;Agree. I just thought that some other editors have the same default. _ The extra whitespace waisting without much gain is the stronger argument.
gromacs~master~Ia1880f5670714c497f683be10a9e72b505ca6c5a;e0732ba1b116a0929696e6523168900b491c0b3c;.clang-format;3;0;0;AccessModifierOffset: -4;I have no preference. I just want to suggest to not use the emacs argument to decide. I don't think you should use emacs builtin formatter together with clang-format. Rather it is better to just configure emacs to use clang-format for its in editor formatting. Reason is that even with this change you have many subtle differences and it is really annoying if emacs tries to reformat it different from clang-format.
