gromacs~master~Ibd2a88768eba25c4836b8f692fd9d61e8960e073;9f50783d21dd2d595aa2a4bab4a5efc5527db237;src/gromacs/math/densityfit.cpp;344;0;0;           * (covarianceSqrt / sqrt(helperValues.comparisonSquaredSum))_;Not returning  helperValues.covariance / (sqrt(ref) * sqrt(comp)), because this turned out to be less stable numerically. _  _ The documentation states explicitly the equation that underlies this measure and it should be clear from that.
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;93;0;0; * \brief Describes work that is constant for the lifetime of a decomposition.;This constant is confusing. Work that is constant over the whole simulation is also constant over the lifetime of a decomposition.
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;93;0;0; * \brief Describes work that is constant for the lifetime of a decomposition.;What wording do you suggest that meas the intent more clear? _ "work that changes between decomposison" _ "work that has the lifetime of a decomposition" _ "work descriptor flags constant for the lifetime of a decomposition, but might change across decomposition phases"
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;93;0;0; * \brief Describes work that is constant for the lifetime of a decomposition.;I'm waiting for suggestions on this, if "constant" is confusing let's try to come up with a better a way to express this.
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;93;0;0; * \brief Describes work that is constant for the lifetime of a decomposition.;Describes the work done on this domain on every step of its lifetime, based on the _ current particle interactions, but which might change after the next domain partitioning. _  _ An object....
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;93;0;0; * \brief Describes work that is constant for the lifetime of a decomposition.;Thanks. Took a combination of the two. Also change StepWorkload docs to follow a similar wording.
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;93;0;0; * \brief Describes work that is constant for the lifetime of a decomposition.;Describes the work done on this domain on every step of its lifetime, other than _ work described by a SimulationWorkload object. _  _ This work description is based the SimulationWorkload in the context of the _ current particle interactions assigned to this domain. The latter might change after _ the next domain partitioning. _  _ An object....
gromacs~master~I17bf3ec25a3ffb329f225f54cc4217956cbb3ec2;eb5ef3cb6e5e7aba3062c643468fd271babb7f07;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;125;0;0; * simulation.;, and independent of the particle interactions handled on any specific domain
