gromacs~master~Iba40387f065e6fae2551540136e925f7c764d6aa;bbd00d41066b52901e2b1775d30e8c001bd86107;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;131;0;0; * simulation.;see here
gromacs~master~Iba40387f065e6fae2551540136e925f7c764d6aa;bbd00d41066b52901e2b1775d30e8c001bd86107;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidesimulationworkload.cpp;74;0;0;    simulationWorkload.haveEwaldSurfaceContribution = haveEwaldSurfaceContribution_;No, that was not the intent. The intent was that only those flags are stored in either of these data structures that can change when the entity they are associated to expires, but not those that (always) have a lifetime that matches (or exceeds) that of a higher-level data structure. Consequently,  _ if haveEwaldSurfaceCorrection can not change across DD/search phases, it should only be included in simulationWorkload.
gromacs~master~Iba40387f065e6fae2551540136e925f7c764d6aa;bbd00d41066b52901e2b1775d30e8c001bd86107;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidesimulationworkload.cpp;74;0;0;    simulationWorkload.haveEwaldSurfaceContribution = haveEwaldSurfaceContribution_;But then the documentation of DomainLifetimeWorkload is not fully accurate. _ And then we should pass all three workloads to the force calculation so they can be used to trigger the calculations.
gromacs~master~Iba40387f065e6fae2551540136e925f7c764d6aa;bbd00d41066b52901e2b1775d30e8c001bd86107;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidesimulationworkload.cpp;74;0;0;    simulationWorkload.haveEwaldSurfaceContribution = haveEwaldSurfaceContribution_;The original vision should be in the struct doxygen, and was intended at one point to capture values that were constant over predictable durations
gromacs~master~Iba40387f065e6fae2551540136e925f7c764d6aa;bbd00d41066b52901e2b1775d30e8c001bd86107;src/gromacs/taskassignment/decidesimulationworkload.cpp;74;0;0;    simulationWorkload.haveEwaldSurfaceContribution = haveEwaldSurfaceContribution_;Are you referring to the following sentence: _  _  ...because that can be set up _  once per simulation or neighborlist lifetime and not changed _  thereafter. _  _ That is residual content from the original PpWorkload data structure which I failed to properly reword. _ DomainLifetimeWorkload should hold data that is: _ - constant for the lifetime of the domain, _ - but may change across decomposition/search phases. _  _ SimulationWorkload has data constant during the entire run, hence it can not change across dd/search steps.
