gromacs~master~Ia3bc41c0d0566993166f567409510cf9c9ec2020;4c2e24de5aaaa18ca10a22cadc692c99ad04b70b;cmake/gmxVersionInfo.cmake;457;0;0;    gmx_add_custom_output_target(checksum-files RUN_ALWAYS;When making the tarball, the reference checksum does have to be in the source tree, but that procedure pertains the release mechanism. The generated checksum on the other hand is made during cmake-time, and is associated with a configuration (if nothing else through the detected python and the cmake execution). Beside that logical distinction, running cmake should not modify the source tree, I think.
