gromacs~master~Ied74638d35e74a8970427df712501cd63e0aa0ab;8b4f1fc0a14b87da01c65d2bebe4cf90bb1afa4d;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;1159;0;0;        // If there are vsites, the forces are copied earlier to spread vsite forces on host,;If there are vsites, we should copy the forces earlier and set a per-step flag that forces are already transferred to the host. That boolean should be checked here. Relying on checking vsite in two places creates a bug when we also need them copied earlier for some other reason, change it there, and don't make the matching change here.
gromacs~master~Ied74638d35e74a8970427df712501cd63e0aa0ab;8b4f1fc0a14b87da01c65d2bebe4cf90bb1afa4d;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;1159;0;0;        // If there are vsites, the forces are copied earlier to spread vsite forces on host,;> Also, since the H2D and D2H copies are managed by the StatePropagatorDataGpu, we can move this logic there _  _ Such a boolean is probably best stored in StatePropagatorDataGpu, I think. However, the challenge remains in keeping the flag consistent -- which isn't necessarily less tricky than keeping two conditions in sync, not without having all flags centralized (including output etc.) and generating flags for nstlist steps ahead. For efficiency, when we mature this code, we will have to use flags and conditions across not just  translation units, but MD steps too_ e.g. launch x D2H right after update if the next step needs coordinates.  _  _ >  (e.g. by making separate copyForVSites/copyForOutput methods). _ > The latter can combine coordinates/velocities/forces depending on what is needed. _  _ What we need to keep in mind is that we need to write code that later could be the basis of generating a task graph. From that point of view, it does not matter which CPU task requests the forces, the only thing that matter is that: _ - if any task needs forces D2H has to be enqueued -- which itself should IMO be done right after the force reduction kernel, in a single place_ _ - wait for the force D2H to complete before the consumer task. _  _ We are not doing this because we wrote code in a simplistic way by launching D2H and immediately waiting. We should move away from this asap (post beta2), for most cases when possible -- because we can't can't call do_per_step() in do_force(), output will likely need to be done separately (hence we'll need multiple D2H launches and a mechanism to track them).
gromacs~master~Ied74638d35e74a8970427df712501cd63e0aa0ab;8b4f1fc0a14b87da01c65d2bebe4cf90bb1afa4d;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;1159;0;0;        // If there are vsites, the forces are copied earlier to spread vsite forces on host,;stepWork is a const and can't be modified here. Having a pre-defined bool there is as bad as using vsites != nullptr. I will add a NOTE here and in do_force, posting that we should be careful with this copy in order not to overwrite the forces. As noted in the TODO below, there should be single D2H copy call, right after force computation is done on the GPU. Also, since the H2D and D2H copies are managed by the StatePropagatorDataGpu, we can move this logic there (e.g. by making separate copyForVSites/copyForOutput methods). The latter can combine coordinates/velocities/forces depending on what is needed.
gromacs~master~Ied74638d35e74a8970427df712501cd63e0aa0ab;8b4f1fc0a14b87da01c65d2bebe4cf90bb1afa4d;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;1162;0;0;        //       copy when vsites are on or when the update is not offloaded, which is not done in do_force(...);the multiple negatives make this hard to read. can you rephrase?
