gromacs~master~Ied74638d35e74a8970427df712501cd63e0aa0ab;21a5a8d7d7e80ae2790fa488dd5280a643fc92e4;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;1179;1175;1179;        if (runScheduleWork->stepWork.useGpuFBufferOps && !vsite && do_per_step(step, ir->nstfout));I think the issue that this overwrites the forces which on GPU buffer ops steps (w/o GPU update) are the result of: the D2H on sim_util.cpp:1767 + pme_receive_force_ener() accumulating separate PME rank forces into it. _  _ The above condition has useGpuFBufferOps while the one on sim_util.cpp:1764 refers to !useGpuUpdate -- something I noted before just did not get to identifying how will that go wrong. Luckily the test caught it. AFAICT we should have simulationWork.useGpuUpdate here too.
