gromacs~master~Iebb184dc2e0b5fb68b4a627314d2373391c6ebf9;557bb12e4752dbc97309b2444a4b445617347a20;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;796;0;0;    domainWork.haveCpuForces          = domainWork.haveSpecialForces || domainWork.haveCpuListedForceWork || domainWork.haveFreeEnergyWork_;Having thought more about this, this should be a haveLocalCpuForceWork which would also include all other offloadable work from simulationWorkload. Additionally, we already have something like that (haveCpuLocalForces on line 1578). We should unify these here or in follow-up.
gromacs~master~Iebb184dc2e0b5fb68b4a627314d2373391c6ebf9;557bb12e4752dbc97309b2444a4b445617347a20;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;823;0;0;                (runScheduleWork->domainWork.haveCpuForces) ||;> but i will need to move the domainWork initialization to before the the GPU buffers are reallocated. I suggest we submit this fix to have the single-gpu case working. _  _ That won't work as setupDomainLifetimeWorkload() can only be done nbnxn_put_on_grid_*() in the current setup. _  _ As suggested offline, to avoid blocking the fix and the beta, let's create two disjoint set of conditions (or three if we separate output from search) for the the points where coordiantes need to be D2H'd and improve in follow up. _  _ We can add a single one or two in do_force() because at search we always need to copy, only on non-search steps do we have to access domainWorkload, so at the beginning of do_force() we can write _  _   if (!stepWork.doNeighborSearch && (domainWork.haveLocalCpuForceWork)) _   { _     // launch copy _   }
gromacs~master~Iebb184dc2e0b5fb68b4a627314d2373391c6ebf9;557bb12e4752dbc97309b2444a4b445617347a20;src/gromacs/mdtypes/simulation_workload.h;120;0;0;        bool haveCpuForces = false_;Somewhat out of scope for this patch, but the first three bools refer to "work," which seems to be usefully vague because we might some day have an MC engine and the work won't always include forces. haveCpuListedForceWork seems inconsistent with that approach. And haveCpuForces seems even more inconsistent. Prefer they become haveCpuListedWork and haveCpuWork, respectively.
