gromacs~master~Idaed4da41bf5b72435c47bab8aeb7130b36b03c7;38f66a5e9a3f1ff5e35e4c1065b7ad6369f1a6fc;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;796;0;0;    domainWork.haveCpuLocalForces     = (domainWork.haveSpecialForces || domainWork.haveCpuListedForceWork || stepWork.useCpuPmeFReduction ||;haveCpuLocalForces = ... || useCpuPmeFReduction || ..._ _ doesn't make sense, it must be a bug or leftover from some intermediate code. useCpuPmeFReduction can never be true when useGpuForcesHaloExchange is true as when we offload PME, we also always do GPU-side reduction AFAICT. _  _ I suggest simply omitting useCpuPmeFReduction here.
gromacs~master~Idaed4da41bf5b72435c47bab8aeb7130b36b03c7;38f66a5e9a3f1ff5e35e4c1065b7ad6369f1a6fc;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;796;0;0;    domainWork.haveCpuLocalForces     = (domainWork.haveSpecialForces || domainWork.haveCpuListedForceWork || stepWork.useCpuPmeFReduction ||;This should be haveCpuLocalForceWork which should include simulationWorkload flags that indicate whether there is GPU PME and GPU Nonbonded work (for the sake of completeness). _  _ haveCpuLocalForces, if we really need it should be in stepWork, but I need to think it through why have we created this complicated link between PME offload, GPU f buffer ops linked indirectly to this flag which seems to indicate whether there have been local forces computed on the CPU -- this seems entirely unnecessary (unless I'm missing some complicated link to separate PME rank direct GPU comm). _  _ Alan, any thoughts?
