gromacs~master~If668366b76d49f7b624eedb501f8af19135c4386;1d5e6239dc348b0611f759359cf4fe1e2c0c1ba5;src/gromacs/mdrun/runner.cpp;1238;0;0;        (devFlags.enableGpuHaloExchange || devFlags.enableGpuPmePPComm));Currently this logic means that if the peer access setup fails, then a warning is issued. We need to leave a TODO here, so that when we make this available in non-developer builds that we need to decide whether it is appropriate from a performance *and* usability consideration to warn and continue, or instead issue an error and stop. If we want the former behavior, then we need to provide a way for the user to configure gmx / run mdrun so that they do not get habituated to ignoring warnings. Otherwise, we need to change the implementation to use the error stream, and fail.
