gromacs~master~I4463de3266d97c5f91bac65d3d997cf564e6e880;a2ef644a5f2c96d17903be1d070c09ae1f664109;src/gromacs/mdrun/runner.cpp;179;178;179;    //! If true, forces 'mdrun -update auto' default to 'gpu';I did not quite get what you mean. Right now the behavior is: _ -update cpu and auto both completely ignore the GPU path _ -update gpu exits with assertion failure _ With this env. variable: _ -update cpu ignores the GPU path _ -update auto switches to GPU path if possible _ -update gpu exits with assertion failure _ Should this be changed?
gromacs~master~I4463de3266d97c5f91bac65d3d997cf564e6e880;a2ef644a5f2c96d17903be1d070c09ae1f664109;src/gromacs/mdrun/runner.cpp;179;178;179;    //! If true, forces 'mdrun -update auto' default to 'gpu';ok, this should work then. But I still don't think the documentation is correct, as the rest of the -update auto behaviour is still the same, as it doesn't force anything to run on the GPU, It only makes it possible instead of hard coding that update runs on the CPU
gromacs~master~I4463de3266d97c5f91bac65d3d997cf564e6e880;a2ef644a5f2c96d17903be1d070c09ae1f664109;src/gromacs/mdrun/runner.cpp;179;178;179;    //! If true, forces 'mdrun -update auto' default to 'gpu';That is the intended behavior, so  I don't see an issue. We need the "auto" to default to CPU for unsupported cases but default to GPU for the supported ones to be able to test using the existing script. Either somebody needs to change gmxtest or this is IMO the right way to move forward and be able to test with GPU update.
gromacs~master~I4463de3266d97c5f91bac65d3d997cf564e6e880;42bae4a6fd134db8c74a1bb2e3f49c1d5092895f;/COMMIT_MSG;7;0;0;Refs. #3163.;This should change the meaning of -update auto, not force the update to GPU, i.e. -update auto will still map to "on" only if the settings are supported.
gromacs~master~I4463de3266d97c5f91bac65d3d997cf564e6e880;42bae4a6fd134db8c74a1bb2e3f49c1d5092895f;/COMMIT_MSG;7;0;0;Refs. #3163.;this is not what I intended here. the variable should only allow update to run on GPU, but not force it. forcing will not work with the current testing setup
