gromacs~master~Ic9e1eb988bc9c934eb8e9cd6009008e6e60d8342;9b5070cb5a1d0f947417ace7d62ce359389e6ad0;python_packaging/src/gmxapi/simulation/mdrun.py;316;315;316;        # We have no way to query the name of the trajectory produced, and we;This is not very nice and IMO a regression in functionality. I understand that keeping track of the file names probably means there needs to be some kind of state that outlives single 'runs' of gmxapi mdrun in order to play nicely with workflows, but specifying the output is a pretty key functionality from a user perspective.
gromacs~master~Ic9e1eb988bc9c934eb8e9cd6009008e6e60d8342;9b5070cb5a1d0f947417ace7d62ce359389e6ad0;python_packaging/src/gmxapi/simulation/mdrun.py;316;315;316;        # We have no way to query the name of the trajectory produced, and we;gmxapi.simulation.mdrun is currently less functional and flexible than the 0.0.7 version, but I don't see that this change is a regression over 0.1b1 functionality... Are you asking for an additional feature to specify the output file name or location? I am reluctant to add a catch-all input to handle all CLI mdrun options without more integration (so that the API knows what they *mean*), and I really don't want to enshrine file naming in the API, but we could add a keyword argument to the mdrun helper function that would override the default trajectory file name. Is that the sort of thing you are talking about?
gromacs~master~Ic9e1eb988bc9c934eb8e9cd6009008e6e60d8342;9b5070cb5a1d0f947417ace7d62ce359389e6ad0;python_packaging/src/gmxapi/simulation/mdrun.py;316;315;316;        # We have no way to query the name of the trajectory produced, and we;I agree that we need to be able to specify names for input and output, but getting access to the output trajectory is all that is needed for now. _ One question, how would this interact with the basic function to run just a command line tool and I overwrite the filename there?
gromacs~master~Ic9e1eb988bc9c934eb8e9cd6009008e6e60d8342;9b5070cb5a1d0f947417ace7d62ce359389e6ad0;python_packaging/src/gmxapi/simulation/mdrun.py;316;315;316;        # We have no way to query the name of the trajectory produced, and we;The full CLI arguments should be available if `gmx mdrun` is invoked by wrapping the command line tool instead of using the bindings, if that's what you're asking. The current package executes all commandline_operation work in the same directory. It is possible to implement safety checks to avoid writing multiple files with the same name, but such checks do not yet exist. gmxapi.operation.mdrun work is executed in separate subdirectories as a first step in compartmentalizing side effects of individual operations. One of the reasons to separate the execution of an operation from the naming of files is to let the API distinguish between working files (implementation details) and results.
gromacs~master~Ic9e1eb988bc9c934eb8e9cd6009008e6e60d8342;9b5070cb5a1d0f947417ace7d62ce359389e6ad0;python_packaging/src/gmxapi/simulation/mdrun.py;316;0;0;        # have avoided exposing the ability to specify it, so we have to assume;yes, that was my question. thanks for clarifying :)
