gromacs~master~I5b1cff1846c7c3bd966b6bf9c0af72769600ef18;cef79f5459e15b3678822dfaa24745b1b1cc3c24;src/gromacs/mdlib/sim_util.cpp;1550;1544;1550;    if (PAR(cr) && !thisRankHasDuty(cr, DUTY_PME));This should not be moved that introduces a penalty on non direct comm code-paths. _  _ As I see it both to avoid such a regression as well as to avoid emulating MPI blocking synchronous behavior we need to split the launch sync/wait by introducing: _ - a function that does only async launch transfer + record event (at the earliest convenient point) _ - async enqueue wait prior to GPU reduction launch _ - blocking wait before launching the CPU reduction _  _ The latter two will both need the event associated with the launch, so the current streamSycn can be replaced with an GpuEventSynchronizer.waitForEvent().
