gromacs~master~Ifb2e4af256282340f1111262f91e5d73d93c3208;ef71157bba94755dd8f191e89b530cfd03a102d4;docs/reference-manual/special/density-guided-simulation.rst;201;199;201;constant is adapted by scaling with :math:`1+1/tau`. Note that adaptive force;It might be nice to say something here about how this is technically a weak coupling algorithm. Since the state "average particle positions matches those in some density" may not be in the ensemble, the forces being very high suggests one of the following _ the system and the density are from different ensembles (wrong coordinates) _ the system and density are in the same ensemble but the system is prepared in such a way that the system ensemble cannot remain stationary (bad starting configuration)
