gromacs~master~I0181ff67065c75f20cddc361f695df9bf888cd88;312ed19965a3d69f67956291e19507eefc921280;src/gromacs/ewald/pme_pp_comm_gpu_impl.cu;103;0;0;    nbLocalSync.enqueueWaitEvent(nbLocalStream_)_;Hmmm. Having looked at it again, I actually think we instead need a cudaStreamSynchronize here when recieving to the CPU, since they forces are reduced on the CPU when the method returns. (This is equivalent to the MPI_Recv blocking in the original path).Point noted for the GPU case.
