gromacs~master~I0181ff67065c75f20cddc361f695df9bf888cd88;f3d6b867d3dd489e9e04a52fe94a2d1e77a8110d;src/gromacs/ewald/pme_only.cpp;666;0;0;            bool useGpuFPmeReduction = pme_pp->useGpuDirectComm_;Ack - Renamed boolean to suppressForceD2H.
gromacs~master~I0181ff67065c75f20cddc361f695df9bf888cd88;f3d6b867d3dd489e9e04a52fe94a2d1e77a8110d;src/gromacs/ewald/pme_only.cpp;666;0;0;            bool useGpuFPmeReduction = pme_pp->useGpuDirectComm_;> But this flag controls the PME task side of the transfer, which can always be perfomed from the GPU (hence we have *GPU*->CPU or *GPU*->GPU). _  _ Ack. _  _ I see now the issue: we've not done the necessary refactoring that i) configures PME for the next nstlist steps ii) decouples pme_gpu_launch_gather() from the launch of the transfers and therefore we now need to pass around this boolean everywhere. _  _ I'll see if we can arrange these in a better way, but in the meantime I suggest to avoid the reassignment or at least rename this boolean as the PME rank should have nothing to do with how the PP rank will reduce forces.
