gromacs~master~I0181ff67065c75f20cddc361f695df9bf888cd88;5c615e1548924e43dceb9f630620c217d45da6b3;src/gromacs/ewald/pme_pp.cpp;391;0;0;void gmx_pme_receive_f(t_forcerec *fr,;The proper solution is an object PmePpComm that understands the required behavior, either such a boolean data member, or in its type (e.g. we make the Impl class of type PmePpCommGpu or PmePpCommCpu). The issue here is that nobody ever did that for PmePpComm, so there's nowhere to store such booleans now. _  _ Even if we always make PmePpCommGpu and put the boolean inside it, that means the logic of line 374 has to be inside it, and now we've implemented PmePpComm, not the GPU variant. I'm open to doing that in future, but it shouldn't block us now. _  _ Agree such a flag needs to be in SimulationWorkload to control how we make and configure the PmePpCommThing.
