gromacs~master~I66aeeaea54931398b1a4a30b920b092f7d40ae16;4c9d561f0403dd5f5635aebb0eedf47492f33c67;src/gromacs/ewald/pme_only.cpp;564;0;0;        stateGpu = std::make_unique<gmx::StatePropagatorDataGpu>(commandStream, deviceContext, GpuApiCallBehavior::Async, paddingSize)_;The main value of this change is to move the point where we make some streams unusable closer to the point of use. That's a minor improvement, and perhaps worth the work of doing it. _  _ The real issue here is that the StatePropagatorDataGpu is too general for use on a PME-only rank, which is what is creating the concern that there are streams, methods and constructors inappropriate to use on such a rank. There should be a PmeOnlyRankManager thing that has the stream and context it needs to direct the management of the required buffers.
