gromacs~master~Ieca885d935aa1e0d592735bc7027f8261288b635;7723f74c90f0668094094b9eb266cc0000de152f;src/gromacs/mdrun/md.cpp;324;320;324;        GMX_RELEASE_ASSERT(ir->eI == eiMD, "Only md integrator is supported on the GPU.")_;@Artem It's better design to implement these as part of the construction logic, so related things are in the same place. That will mean we need to pass ed to UpdateConstrainCuda(), which anyway we'd need if we'd implement support for ED. Also, the strings should be usefully specific and consistent with other usages, e.g. "Only the md integrator can run the update task on the GPU," so that if a user would ever see one, we have fewer people thinking wrong things like "Oh, to get virtual sites, I have to build a non-gpu mdrun"
