gromacs~master~Ia33e366f32d777ec980940ff7e284ab0b3498637;50f2cc17246dceba74e22a3f9e9e030b0bd308fe;src/gromacs/mdtypes/state_propagator_data_gpu_impl_gpu.cpp;241;0;0;    switch (atomLocality);Then we should have multiple such EnumerationArrays such that velocitiesTransferStreams_[AtomLocality::NonLocal] is initialized to nullptr and we can assert the same thing everywhere (ie that the locality selected for this kind of copy operation has a valid stream). _  _ PS 30 duplicated the choosing logic in both places where a copy using that choice is implemented. My proposal puts the choosing logic in one place, and implements a copy using that choice in two places.
gromacs~master~Ia33e366f32d777ec980940ff7e284ab0b3498637;50f2cc17246dceba74e22a3f9e9e030b0bd308fe;src/gromacs/mdtypes/state_propagator_data_gpu_impl_gpu.cpp;241;0;0;    switch (atomLocality);I tend to think that the improvement is not huge if any -- sure its a bit fewer lines of code but there is a considerable drawback in that we have to split logic of picking a stream assertion of what is a valid locality for the respective copy. This is trivial here (as only Count is invalid), but elsewhere it won't be, e.g. for velocities NonLocal won't be valid -- so we'll have to assign nullptr in the constructor and separately in a totally different but logically related code context in copyVelocitiesToGpu, we'll have to assert that AtomLocality::NonLocal is not valid.
gromacs~master~Ia33e366f32d777ec980940ff7e284ab0b3498637;50f2cc17246dceba74e22a3f9e9e030b0bd308fe;src/gromacs/mdtypes/state_propagator_data_gpu_impl_gpu.cpp;241;0;0;    switch (atomLocality);Yes! I even had a small patch that I shared a little while ago: https://gerrit.gromacs.org/#/c/gromacs/+/13422/
